  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 8, P = 22. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[12, 3, 8, 11, 2, 1, 5, 5], [21, 18, 4, 8, 4, 21, 19, 0], [2, 12, 14, 5, 10, 12, 12, 0]], sigma = [1, 0, 3, 2, 5, 4, 7, 6], B = [20, 20, 9, 9, 17, 17, 20, 20].",
